<title>POLAND: Sberbank tops Polish paper's banking poll.</title>
<headline>Sberbank tops Polish paper's banking poll.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's biggest bank, Sberbank, placed first and Czech Komercni Banka second in a ranking of Eastern and Central European banks by the Polish monthly Home and Market, the magazine said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the Russian foreign trade bank Rosvneshtorgbank ranked third and the Polish state-owned agricultural Bank Gospodarki Zywnosciowej (BGZ) bank fourth in the poll that took into account capital, assets and financial results.</p>
<p>Ceska Sporitelna and Polish Bank Handlowy SA were fifth and sixth respectively.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
